 "evidence": "Two-year GCM tests, one realization each from the design climate's year-19 restart, set against the rh 0.7 branch over the same years from the same restart: the first two years of a spin-up, before the column settles (the branch reached balance by years 8-10), so they show the direction and early size of each change and not its settled climate. The CM1 numbers are the settled boxes (the sea box's third lunar day, the land box's second), forced by Kuo's GCM. The scheme's checks are calculations with the tested Python copy on lunar-day mean columns. The off check compares the GCM's own output and restart bit for bit.",
 "reading_rule": "stages[stage][run]: rain by quarter (sunrise-noon, noon-sunset, sunset-midnight, midnight-sunrise; mm/day, all rain and the convective part) at the Near-side Sea's six cells and the land box's cells; upper_air.at_heights_k the lunar-day mean at the sea cells taken onto the box's levels at equal shares of the surface pressure, at heights_m as box_upper_air does; column_change_k the sea site's lunar-day mean temperature on PlaSim's levels (top first) less the branch's, and global_column_change_k the area mean's; global the yearly summaries' means with the area-mean rain, its convective share and the top two levels (sigma 0.038, 0.119). scheme_checks.convergence: the reference's error against 1,024 steps a layer, the largest below sigma 0.2 and at the top two levels. scheme_checks.cm1_column: the reference minus the box's air on PlaSim's levels and at the heights, beside box_upper_air's zero-buoyancy plumes (plume minus box)."
